+- **One owner per entity:** `entity_memberships.owner_seq` is a stored generated column that is `1` when `role = 'owner'` and `NULL` for every other role. The unique index `entity_memberships_one_owner` on `(entity_id, owner_seq)` lets an entity have many admins/employees (NULLs do not collide) while the database rejects a second owner on both SQLite and MariaDB. Ownership transfer updates roles inside a transaction.
